    "body": "This works for bSize 0, 1, 2 but I think it is buggy for bSize == 3 (meaning \"4 bytes\").\n\nReading this now, it seems confusing to say each item has an \"item data field\", which might be 0 bytes. Intuitively, a report field that occupies 0 bytes in the report isn't actually in the report. Perhaps we should refactor this to clarify that an item has an item data value, which is either populated by the item data field (if bSize > 0) or is zero (if bSize == 0).",
